# MedSync Health, Inc.
## Infrastructure Overview
**Document ID**: OPS-001
**Classification**: Internal
**Last Updated**: January 2025

---

## Infrastructure Summary

MedSync operates a multi-region cloud infrastructure on AWS, designed for high availability, security, and scalability. Our infrastructure supports 589 customers, 85 million patient records, and processes over 50 million transactions daily.

---

## Architecture Overview

### High-Level Architecture

| Layer | Technology | Purpose |
|-------|------------|---------|
| Edge | CloudFront, WAF | CDN, DDoS protection |
| Load Balancing | ALB, NLB | Traffic distribution |
| Compute | EKS (Kubernetes) | Application workloads |
| Database | Aurora PostgreSQL | Primary data store |
| Cache | ElastiCache Redis | Performance, sessions |
| Search | OpenSearch | Full-text search |
| Data Warehouse | Snowflake | Analytics |
| Queue | SQS, Kafka | Async processing |
| Storage | S3 | Object storage |

### Regional Deployment

| Region | Purpose | Services |
|--------|---------|----------|
| us-east-1 (Virginia) | Primary | Full stack |
| us-west-2 (Oregon) | Secondary | Full stack (DR) |
| eu-west-1 (Ireland) | DR/Future EU | Warm standby |

